title: gamescript
---
<<declare $YarnTalkedElder = false>>
<<declare $crateTries = 0>>
<<declare $warnPerson = "">>
	Josh: ...
===


title: square_initial
---
	Josh: What's up Amos?
	Elder Amos: Hmm, fine, I'm fine, yes. How about you, Josh?
	Josh: I'm good. Kind of a misty day, don't you think?
	Elder Amos: Yes, misty indeed.
	Josh: Yeah.
	Elder Amos: ...
	Josh: Ok... good talk, I guess.
	<<set $YarnTalkedElder = true>>
===
title: square_marcus_erika
---
	Marcus: What's up Joshy?
	Josh: 'Sup.
	Erika: Wow, look who's in a good mood today.
	Josh: Yup, can barely contain myself.
	Marcus: Ah, come on man, it's a beautiful day! Everyone's having fun, doing their things.
	// A pergunta sobre o Elder so existe se o Josh JA falou com ele — e por isso ela e a
	// primeira metade de uma fala do Josh, nao uma fala solta: sem a condicional ele
	// termina em "You have a weird concept of beauty." e a Erika emenda direto.
	<<if $YarnTalkedElder is true>>
		Josh: You have a weird concept of beauty. Anyway... have you talked to Amos? He seems a bit off.
		Marcus: Ah, old man's been off for some time now, nothing new.
		Erika: Forget that fossil, what are we doing today?
	<<else>>
		Josh: You have a weird concept of beauty.
		Erika: So, what are we doing today?
	<<endif>>
	Josh: I'm heading home I guess.
	Marcus: Come on Joshy, you know my time is due here.
	Josh: <i>He's really leaving...</i>
	Erika: Don't be a shut in for once, Josh.
	Josh: Ok, ok...I'll just relax for a bit. Meet you here in an hour-ish.
	Marcus: Nice, okay.
	Erika: Don't know why you need to "relax" right now, but ok.
	<<progress TalkedFriends>>
===
title: not_talked_friends
---
Josh: I should talk to my friends.
<<progress NotTalkedFriendsYet>>
===
title: home_outside_noise
---
// Trigger na CURVA da estrada (box "NoiseOnTheRoad").
// Nao tem `movement` nenhum: o jogador andou ate aqui sozinho e continua andando
// sozinho depois. O DialogueStarter congela e descongela ele automaticamente.
//
// O ruido e SOM, nao caixa de dialogo: nada de um falante chamado "Noise". O
// `playsound` dispara junto com a fala de propósito — nao poe `wait` antes da
// primeira linha do no, porque o LinePresenter so tem o alpha zerado no fim do
// dialogo anterior e o texto velho continua no campo, entao a espera pisca a fala
// passada na tela.
//
// Falta so registrar o clipe: DialogueManager > Sounds > entrada com Sound Name =
// NoiseOnTheRoad. Enquanto nao existir, o PlaySound so loga "Sound not found" e o
// dialogo segue normal.
//
// A guarda existe pra que o ruido nunca reapareca depois do encontro com o Haze,
// mesmo que as Conditions do DialogueStarter estejam mal preenchidas ou que a cena
// recarregue (o OnceTime do DialogueStarter e por instancia, morre no reload).
<<if not hasprogress("HeardNoise") and not hasprogress("MetHaze")>>
<<playsound NoiseOnTheRoad>>
Josh: Hm? What's that noise?
<<progress HeardNoise>>
<<endif>>
===

title: home_outside_first
---
// Trigger PERTO DE CASA (box "OutsideHouseHaze"). De novo sem `movement Josh...`:
// ele para onde o jogador parou. Por isso todo `face` daqui aponta para o OBJETO
// (`face Josh HazeOne`) e nao para um lado fixo — de qualquer angulo de chegada o
// MC fica virado pro Haze.
<<enable HazeOne>>
// Ele desce olhando pro lado pra onde anda (esquerda) e so vira pro Josh quando para
// — foi o que ficou melhor no teste. Por isso o `face` vem DEPOIS do movimento, e o
// movimento nao leva modificador nenhum.
// (Pro contrario — virado pro Josh o trajeto inteiro — e por o `face` ANTES e escrever
// `movement HazeFloatDown hold freeze`: "hold" = anda sem virar.)
<<movement HazeFloatDown freeze>>
<<face HazeOne Josh>>
<<face Josh HazeOne>>
Josh: What's this?!
<<movement HazeEnter freeze>>
<<face HazeOne Josh>>
<<face Josh HazeOne>>
?: Hello sir.
Josh: Wha—who...what are you?!
?: Hmm... I'm me I guess, I don't know.
Josh: Ok? And what are you doing here?
?: Nothing in particular.
Josh: Ok just—come inside or else you'll freak people out.
?: Why would I freak them out?
Josh: Have you looked at yourself in the mirror?
// Aqui existia um `movement HazeApproach freeze`, que mandava o Haze pro marcador
// fixo HazeFloat. Isso so funcionava quando o Josh era colocado no PlayerApproach por
// um `movement`: agora que o JOGADOR anda ate a casa sozinho, o Josh para a esquerda
// do HazeFloat, e o Haze "andava pro outro lado" no meio da conversa. Ele ja esta cara
// a cara desde o HazeEnter, entao fica parado falando ate entrar na casa no HazeLeave.
?: I have not.
Josh: Yeah, figures.
?: Do i look good?
Josh: Just go on in man.
?: Oookay!
// Era HazeRun (ate WalkHome (2), no chao) e SO DEPOIS HazeLeave (ate WalkHome (1), a
// porta) — dai o "desce e depois sobe". Um movimento so, direto pra porta: o
// MoveTowards do Cutscener anda em linha reta, entao sai na diagonal.
// Se ficar lento, sobe o Speed do HazeLeave no Inspector (o HazeRun era 4, esse e 2).
<<movement HazeLeave freeze>>
<<disable HazeOne>>
Josh: <i>This is going to be a</i> long <i>day.</i>
<<progress MetHaze>>
===

title: home_inside_first
---
// O Haze NAO passeia pela casa. Ele entra, fica parado conversando, vai UMA vez ate a
// TV, volta pro lugar em que entrou pra falar "You're weird", e dali nao sai mais ate
// ir embora. Todos os `movement HazeWander1/2/3` foram removidos por isso.
//
// O `movement JoshHouse freeze` tambem saiu: no Inspector ele esta com o Target
// VAZIO, entao nunca moveu ninguem — so logava warning.
//
// O HazeHouse usa o marcador FIXO HazeSpawn (nao o Player com deslocamento): a sala e
// pequena e o ponto certo e "a ponta do tapete", que se acerta a olho arrastando o
// marcador na cena. Com destino = Player e deslocamento zero, o Haze anda pra DENTRO
// do Josh — foi o que aconteceu.
//
// Geometria: Josh (-134.37, 88.41) | HazeSpawn (-132.86, 88.48) a direita dele |
// TVPlace (-130.30, 89.63) acima e a direita | ExitHouse (-133.87, 86.62) abaixo e a
// esquerda. Todas as viradas saem certas so pela direcao de viagem, sem "flip".
<<enable HazeTwo>>
<<movement HazeHouse freeze>>
<<face HazeTwo Josh>>
<<face Josh HazeTwo>>
?: Wow your home is so pretty!
Josh: It really isn't.
?: Then why are you here?
Josh: Nowhere to go, I guess.
?: That's sad.
// Vai ate a TV e fica olhando pra ela (a TV esta a direita, entao a direcao de viagem
// ja deixa ele virado pro lado certo).
<<movement HazeTV freeze>>
<<face Josh HazeTwo>>
?: A TV! What are you watching?
Josh: I <i>was</i> going to watch some National Geographic before you came in.
?: National Geographic?
Josh: It's a channel that shows anima—
?: Boooring.
Josh: ... Yeah, it is.
// Vira pro Josh, anda ate ele, e so entao fala. Mesmo destino do HazeHouse, entao ele
// para exatamente onde estava quando entrou.
<<face HazeTwo Josh>>
<<movement HazeHouse freeze>>
<<face HazeTwo Josh>>
<<face Josh HazeTwo>>
?: You're weird.
Josh: I'm weird? Says the orange floating thing that appeared out of nowhere. Look—who are you anyway, man? Why are you even here?
?: As I said, I don't know!
Josh: I'm guessing you don't have a name, also.
?: Not that I can remember, no.
Josh: Ok then. I'll call you Haze for now. Call me Josh.
Haze: ... Ok.
Josh: So, you really have no idea how you wound up here?
Haze: Nuh-uh. I feel like I just woke up from a really long nap. Like, reeeeally long.
Josh: Like, how long?
Haze: Feels like it's been forever since I fell asleep, honestly.
Haze: I'm trying to remember, but it's all too messy in my hea—(noise outside)
Josh: Now what?
Haze: Ugh!
Josh: Are you ok?
Haze: I don't know, I felt weird for a second...but it's gone now.
Josh: Good. I'm gonna watch some TV.
Haze: I'm gonna go for a walk!
// Um movimento so, direto pra porta — sai na diagonal, do mesmo jeito que entrou.
<<movement HazeExit freeze>>
<<disable HazeTwo>>
Josh: No you're not, you'll stand out and freak out every—hey, WAIT!
<<progress HazeRanOff>>
<<enable HazeThree>>
// O Marcus e a Erika estavam parados na praca ate aqui. Somem AGORA, com o Josh
// ainda dentro de casa, e nao no comeco do square_haze: desligar o grupo com o
// jogador olhando pra praca seria um pop na tela. "Friends" e o objeto PAI dos
// dois na cena, entao os dois triggers de dialogo da praca (FriendNotTalkedStarter
// e FriendDialogue) saem junto — nao da mais pra conversar com quem nao esta la.
<<disable Friends>>
// O Elder sai de cena no MESMO momento, e pelo mesmo motivo: e agora que ele
// desaparece na historia. O collider e o DialogueStarter dele estao no proprio
// objeto, entao desligar a raiz tira o homem E o gatilho de conversa junto.
<<disable ElderAmos>>
===

title: square_haze
---
// O Haze fica PARADO no meio da estrada, virado pra direita, esperando. O jogador leva
// o Josh ate ele — nao existe `movement` do Josh aqui, e ninguem sai do lugar durante
// a conversa: o `movement HazeStand` (que mexia o Haze no "Ta-dah") e o `movement
// JoshWalk` foram removidos.
//
// O Josh nao faz NADA sozinho aqui. Onde a cena comeca e definido so pelo marcador
// SquareJosh: ele esta no campo "Transformthing" do DialogueStarter, e o trigger se
// recentraliza nele no Start. Arrastar o marcador na cena move o ponto de disparo.
//
// A trava de ordem que voce pediu ja existe, no DialogueStarter deste trigger:
// HasConditions ON, ConditionsCancel OFF, Progress = HazeRanOff. HazeRanOff so e
// setado no fim do home_inside_first, entao cruzar este collider antes da cena de
// dentro de casa nao dispara nada.
// Nao existe `face HazeThree right` aqui de proposito: qualquer correcao de lado na
// primeira linha aparece como um giro na cara do jogador no instante em que a caixa de
// dialogo abre. O lado inicial dele e o estado do OBJETO na cena (SpriteRenderer >
// Flip X desmarcado = olhando pra direita), nao do script.
<<face JoshTwo HazeThree>>
Josh: HEY, wa—huff... huff... wait. Are you insane? Do I have to remind you you're <i>not human</i>?
// O Haze esta de costas pro Josh (olhando pra direita, estrada acima) e so se vira
// quando comeca a responder.
<<face HazeThree JoshTwo>>
Haze: Relax my friend, I found something out! Look.
Haze: Ta-dah!
Josh: ...
Haze: ...
Josh: You know nothing happened right.
Haze: Well, for <i>you</i> it didn't, but that's because you're the only one who can see me right now!
Josh: What? Stop this nonsense dude. Come back to my house and stay there.
<<enable Villager>>
<<movement VillagerEnter freeze>>
Villager: Josh! What are you doing just standing here?
Josh: Uhm... nothing really, I was just... taking a walk. Yes, a walk.
Villager: Taking a walk? Are you insane? Can't you hear the noise coming from Elder Amos' house?
Josh: Oh, yeah. So that's where all the ruckus' coming from.
Villager: Yeah. Anyway, meet everyone there then, after you finish your... walk or whatever. Hurry!
// Entra pela DIREITA andando pra esquerda e sai de volta pela direita, ate fora da
// camera. Sem "flip" nos dois: a virada vem da direcao de viagem, entao ele chega
// olhando pra esquerda (pro Josh) e sai olhando pra direita sozinho.
<<movement VillagerExit>>
Haze: Turns out you're the insane one.
Josh: Shut up.
Haze: Trust me now?
Josh: For this very specific topic, yes.
Haze: Can I go with you, then?
<<disable Villager>>
Josh: ... Ok.
// Troca sem teleporte, sem depender de marcador nenhum:
// 1. o TrueHaze e colocado EXATAMENTE onde o Haze da cutscene esta (mesma posicao,
//    mesmo lado), entao ligar ele nao muda nada na tela;
// 2. o FragmentFollow nao teleporta mais para o lado do jogador quando e ligado —
//    ele caminha ate la sozinho, limitado pelo Max Follow Speed.
<<placeat TrueHaze HazeThree>>
<<disable HazeThree>>
<<enable TrueHaze>>
// O Marcus e a Erika reaparecem na casa do Elder. A ORDEM importa:
// 1. `formation` coloca os dois no FriendsPosition enquanto ainda estao DESLIGADOS,
//    entao nao existe frame nenhum em que eles apareçam no lugar antigo;
// 2. `enable Friends` acende o grupo ja no lugar certo;
// 3. `enable FriendsTalk` liga o trigger do E (fica desligado ate aqui pra nao piscar
//    "E" numa estrada vazia);
// 4. `progress` e o que arma o bark da Erika chamando o Josh na aproximacao.
<<formation FriendsAtEldersHouse>>
<<enable Friends>>
<<enable FriendsTalk>>
<<progress FriendsAtEldersHouse>>
===

title: elders_house_outside
---
Erika: Hey slowpoke.
Marcus: Joshy!
Josh: Hey guys, what happened?
Erika: Basically, Amos disappeared. People are saying they saw him go into the forest.
Josh: Into the forest where, exactly?
Marcus: No one saw, visibility was poor.
Erika: This fucking mist.
Marcus: They are scared, afraid to enter his house. Saying it's cursed.
Josh: What? No one went looking for him?
Erika: They did, but not very far.
Haze: <i>Josh, I feel like we should go in.</i>
Josh: <i>Are you really inside my mind, man?</i>
Haze: <i>Yup.</i>
Josh: <i>Jesus Christ dude, I just wanted to watch some TV...</i>
Josh: </i>Ugh, ok...fine. Why should we go in?</i>
Haze: <i>Just trust me on this one.</i>
Josh: <i>Whatever.</i>
Josh: Ok, I guess I'm going to check his place.
Erika: What, why?
Marcus: What could be inside there?
Josh: I don't know, man. You two have something better to do?
Erika: Why are you so proactive out of nowhere?
Marcus: Who are you and where is our friend Josh?
Josh: Funny. 'Kay, I'm going in.
Erika: I'm also going in, then.
Marcus: Yeah, me too.
Haze: <i>Wouldn't it be better if we went by ourselves?</i>
Josh: <i>Why? It doesn't matter anyway. I'm not stopping them.</i>
Haze: <i>...Okay.</i>
Josh: Let's go, then.
<<progress ElderHouseCutsceneDone>>
===

title: elders_house_inside_explore
---
Josh: What are we looking for, exactly?
Haze: No idea.
Josh: Great.
Marcus: Hmm, food's still good, yeah.
Erika: A Bible... I am out of rolling paper.
===

title: elders_house_bookshelf
---
Haze: Books! Let's see here... "Suddenly, he sits up and tugs my panties off and throws them on the floor. Pulling off his boxer briefs, his erecti—"
Josh: Ok, ok, that's enough.
===

title: elders_house_bookshelf_two
---
Josh: Let's see if there's anything better here... "Desire pools dark and deadly in my—" Yep. No. Old man's a pervert.
Haze: What's a pervert?
Josh: ...
===

title: elders_house_wardrobe
---
Haze: Anything there?
Josh: Nope, it's a mess, can't believe the old man was this disorganized.
===

title: elders_house_writing_table
---
Haze: What are these? Notes?
Josh: Let's see...
Elder Amos: It's been calling to me, calling to me for some time now, calling to me... 
Elder Amos: WHAT SHOULD I DO WHAT SHOULD I DO HELP HELP HELP I NEED TO GO THERE, I NEED TO FIND IT, I NEED TO GET IT IT'S THE ONLY WAY ONLY I CAN DO IT... only I know about it.
Josh: Damn, he was really losing it. What is he talking about?
Haze: There's more down there.
Josh: It's a poem... I can barely read it, must be ages old.
Josh: "North you must go / To get what you need / Through the dark forest path / A new site you shall see"
Josh: "Solve the enigmas therein / Before time runs out / Or else for the land / Ruin will befall"
Josh: Huh... Riddles? What is this, a game? Why was this geezer fooling around with this?
Haze: I guess we need to go North and find out, no?
Josh: Do I really need to find anything out? As far as I know a senile old man got lost in the woods. The only really weird thing here is still you.
Josh: Which leads me to ask... what do you have anything to do with all this?
Haze: ...I'm not sure. I really feel like we need to follow this trail.
Josh: Ok then, let's check it out. I'll talk to Erika and Marcus.
Haze: Should you really tell them? They might notice me.
Josh: Well, they are my best—actually, only, friends. I'd rather be close to them if anything's happening around here. Besides, they'd like you, I think.
Haze: Would they? Let's go then!
Josh: Don't get too excited, an old man just disappeared.
Haze: Oh, yes, of course. That's so sad, I'm sorry.
Josh: Naaah I'm just messing with you man.
Haze: ...
<<progress ReadElderNotes>>
===

title: elders_house_first_floor_call
---
Josh: Kay guys, I found something out, look.
===

title: elders_house_first_floor
---
Marcus: ...
Erika: ...
Marcus: Damn, seems like he was really losing it.
Erika: Holy...
Erika: Ok, so what, we should head North... isn't that the forest right behind this house?
Josh: Yup.
Marcus: I didn't think there was a path there.
Josh: Let's see, maybe we find one.
Marcus: An adventure!
Erika: That's one way to see it.
Josh: ...
<<follow Marcus>>
<<follow Erika>>
===

title: forest_path
---
Marcus: Huh, what do you know? There was really a path!
Erika: Can this even be called a path?
===

title: graveyard
---
Erika: Holy...
Marcus: How was this hidden here all along?
Haze: Did you know about this place, Josh?
Josh: Nope. I know as much as them.
===

title: puzzle_entrance
---
Erika: What the hell is this?
Josh: Probably one of the "enigmas" the old man's poem mentioned.
Marcus: What are those glowing things?
Erika: I kinda want to jump on it.
Marcus: I dare you. You don't have the balls, Eri!
Erika: 50 bucks and I'll—
Josh: Guys can we <i>please</i> focus? How do we solve this?
Marcus: Meh, I suck at puzzles.
Erika: Same. This one's on you, Josh.
Josh: Great, you guys are great.
<<progress PuzzleTalkDone>>
===

title: puzzle_inside
---
Josh: Huh, it's that same statue from Amos'.
Haze: It's calling me...
<<ghosttutorial>>
Erika: What? How did you do that?
Marcus: Way to go Joshy!
Haze: Seems like they didn't notice me...
===

title: josh_confiner
---
Haze: <i>We haven't solved the puzzle yet, Josh!</i>
===

title: haze_confiner
---
Haze: <i>The statue...</i>
===

title: on_first_puzzle_block
---
Haze: <i>I think something's blocking the way.</i>
===

title: crate_refused
---
<<if $crateTries == 0>>
  Haze: I don't think we should do that.
  <<elseif $crateTries == 1>>
  Haze: Why are you still doing that?!
  <<else>>
  Haze: ... I guess...you're stupid.
  Josh: ...
  <<endif>>
  <<set $crateTries = $crateTries + 1>>
  ===

title: raven_conversation
---
Raven: Gawk!
Josh: ...
Raven: ...
<<progress KeyGrabbed>>
===

title: square_signpost
---
Sign: Josh's house: Southwest<br>Elder Amos' house: North
===

// PLACEHOLDER — troca o texto do Haze pela fala que voce quiser.
// Disparado por StatueSwitch > On Refused First Time (so na PRIMEIRA vez
// que a estatua e recusada). As recusas seguintes so piscam o bloqueador.
title: statue_blocked_first
---
Haze: It won't budge. Something's in its way.
Josh: ...the crate?
Haze: Move it and try again.
===
// A conversa final da cripta. Disparada ao PISAR na frente da estatua grande da sala
// do fundo (CryptFinalTalk), nao por E — o beat acontece por chegar la, e nao por
// escolher interagir.
//
// O mapa entra perto do fim, quando eles acham algo atras da estatua: <<sprite>> mostra,
// <<removesprite>> tira. As duas usam a posicao "map", que e um retangulo grande e
// centralizado na cena (MapOverlay > MapSeat).
title: crypt_final
---
Josh: I see something written.
Josh: "The mist is not your friend. It may seem calm and still, but through it malice yearns to grow."
Marcus: What does it mean "it's not your friend?" How can a natural phenomenon be an enemy?
Haze: Agh!
Erika: !
Marcus: !
Josh: What happened?!
Haze: Ugh… I felt weird again.
Erika: Josh, what is that?
Marcus: Yeah Joshy, what the hell is that?
Josh: Guys, Uhm... meet Haze. I don't know what he is.
Erika: …
Marcus: …
Haze: Hi.
Erika: So? That's all you're gonna say about the talking smoke?!
Josh: Huh… yeah, right. So, I found him by my house, I brought him in, and we ended up going together to Amos'. He's the one who helped me with the puzzles.
Marcus: So that's how you did it.
Erika: That explains a lot, but, why are they—I mean, why are <i>you</i> here, Haze? You clearly have something to do with what's going on.
Haze: Honestly…I don't know much. I woke up outside Josh's house, and can't remember anything before that. 
Marcus: Wow…
Marcus: Haze is a good name.
Josh: Right?
Marcus: Crazy stuff happening in our little village!
Erika: I don't know if you should be that excited about it.
Josh: Okay guys, there's more, wait a second.
Josh: "Many have been lost to seal that which now lies below this soil. Its power was just too vast, too incomprehensible. If you were able to solve the challenges and enter this chamber, you hold some of that ancient power in your hands."
Marcus: Ancient power, is he talking about Haze here?
Haze: I don't feel like ancient power.
Marcus: Well, you did that magic back there.
Josh: "That means it is active again, and time is running out. There are two sites within this land where the keys to saving yourself, and everyone you love, are hidden and protected the same way this chamber is.
Josh: "I could not leave them lying around here, for this force is too great to be left unprotected. In the wrong hands, its capacity for harm is beyond measure. I do not know your intentions, I have to be safe. I bid you good luck."
Marcus: Uhm, guys… I'm not finding this <i>that</i> fun anymore.
Erika: Josh… I don't know. Any other day I would laugh at all this, but Amos disappearing? The mist? Talking smoke? I think we need to go after those keys.
Josh: Yeah, I agree.
Marcus: Okay, so now that that's settled, I think some proper introductions are in order. 
Marcus: Hi Haze, I am Marcus, and the beautiful blondie here is Erika. Nice to meet you.
Erika: What's up.
Haze: Nice to meet you guys!
Erika: It seems like you are our key to getting out of this situation.
Haze: Seems like it.
Erika: I just hope you are really on our side.
Marcus: Ah, come on Erika, don't do that. Sorry Haze, she's been like this since kindergarten.
Haze: It's ok, I would also be suspicious of myself. I think. I'm talking smoke, after all.
Josh: Guys, can we talk on the way outta here?
Marcus: Sure, but where do we go?
Haze: There's something more down there!
Josh: Good eye. Let me check.
<<sprite map map>>
Josh: It's a map. Seems like we know where to go now.
<<removesprite map>>
// Branch da apresentacao: avisar a vila ou nao, e quem vai. A ultima fala antes de
// cada "->" e o que a caixa mostra como pergunta em cima das opcoes.
Erika: Guys, I just thought about something... the people in the village don't know about all this... it will be dangerous, but I think someone ought to warn them.
Marcus: I don't know Eri, it could be <i>really</i> dangerous.
Haze: What do you think, Josh?
-> Yes
    // PLACEHOLDER — troca pela fala que voce quiser; e ela que aparece em cima de "Erika / Marcus".
    Josh: Who should go?
    -> Erika
        <<set $warnPerson = "Erika">>
    -> Marcus
        <<set $warnPerson = "Marcus">>
    Josh: I think it's a good idea, {$warnPerson}, can you go? Stay at your house right after, until we pick you up again.
    <<if $warnPerson == "Marcus">>
        Marcus: Sure thing, Joshy.
    <<else>>
        Erika: Ok, but you owe me one.
    <<endif>>
    // Quem vai sai de cena: para de seguir e anda ate a marca CryptExit (fora da tela,
    // no corredor de baixo). Nao bloqueia — o "Ok, let's go" roda enquanto ele anda.
    <<unfollow {$warnPerson}>>
    <<walkto {$warnPerson} CryptExit>>
    Josh: Ok, let's go.
-> No
    Josh: I don't think so guys, it could be unnecessarily dangerous. Let's keep going.
<<progress CryptFinalTalkDone>>
===
